        "explanation": "<p>Assume $\\frac{3x + 5}{(x + 1)(x + 2)} = \\frac{A}{x + 1} + \\frac{B}{x + 2}$.<br><br>Multiply through by $(x + 1)(x + 2)$: $3x + 5 = A(x + 2) + B(x + 1)$.<br><br>Solving for $A$ and $B$: Let $x = -1$, then $3(-1) + 5 = A(1) \\Rightarrow A = 2$.<br>Let $x = -2$, then $3(-2) + 5 = B(-1) \\Rightarrow B = 1$.<br><br>Thus, the partial fractions are $\\frac{2}{x + 1} + \\frac{1}{x + 2}$.</p>",
