        "explanation": "<p>Assume $\\frac{3x + 5}{(x + 1)(x - 2)} = \\frac{A}{x + 1} + \\frac{B}{x - 2}$.<br><br>Multiply through by $(x + 1)(x - 2)$: $3x + 5 = A(x - 2) + B(x + 1)$.<br><br>Solve for $A$ and $B$ by substituting $x = -1$ and $x = 2$:<br><br>For $x = -1$: $3(-1) + 5 = A(-1 - 2) \\Rightarrow 2 = -3A \\Rightarrow A = -\\frac{2}{3}$.<br><br>For $x = 2$: $3(2) + 5 = B(2 + 1) \\Rightarrow 11 = 3B \\Rightarrow B = \\frac{11}{3}$.<br><br>Thus, the partial fractions are $\\frac{-2/3}{x + 1} + \\frac{11/3}{x - 2}$.</p>",
